## 2026-09-30 - MuJoCo RGB-D depth scale and cube visual cleanup
- Purpose: Prevent invalid depth values from entering the cube RGB-D dataset and ROS simulation backend.
- Investigation/optimization: MuJoCo 3.12 depth rendering returned the far clipping distance (~998.65 m with the current scene), while the policy contract expects metric depth bounded to 1.5 m. Clipped/finite conversion was added to the collector and MuJoCo ROS backend; the avoidance scene now uses an explicit cube material and cyan visibility mask.
- Result: Scene physics check and Python syntax checks passed. The local NVIDIA/EGL context still returns blank buffers or stalls because `/dev/nvhost*` and the NVIDIA driver are unavailable; no new dataset or training run was started. ROS tests were not collected from the non-ROS shell.
- Next: Restore the Jetson NVIDIA/EGL runtime, run the 1-episode render probe, then collect and inspect successful RGB-D episodes before conversion.

