## 2026-10-07 - cube best.pt checkpoint integration
- Purpose: Connect the user-provided `Edge_AI/best.pt` cube policy to Big without retraining or recollecting data.
- Investigation/optimization: Converted the Windows-path PyTorch snapshot to `models/vla_cube_best/model.safetensors` with an explicit RGB-only SmolVLA contract; verified checkpoint step 351000, validation loss 0.012969, 1875 episodes/241112 frames, six absolute ROS-radian state/action values, and matching normalization statistics. Separated feedback limits from policy-command limits so the trained gripper range is enforced at `[-1.25, 0]`.
- Result: Big's vendor LeRobot loader loaded the converted checkpoint with `strict=True` on CPU and produced one finite six-joint action from a real dataset RGB frame/state. Registered depth remains mandatory for perception/Safety Gate and is not passed to this RGB-only policy. No camera, detector, GPU or physical-arm success is claimed.
- Next: provide a cube YOLO detector path, then run the MuJoCo route with CUDA restored and inspect proposal-to-Safety-Gate behavior before any hardware run.
